+# A2D2 original Plane runtime
+
+Source baseline: `2f895b82dad839c730c36a5c0cbc046f1e5d6b56` (makeplane/plane).
+This layers local source builds over the upstream Community deployment. The UI,
+API, authentication, permissions, and persistence remain Plane's implementations.
+It does not migrate or modify existing A2D2 Board data.
+
+Run all commands from the repository root. Requires Docker Compose supporting
+`!override` (validated with v5.0.2) and a running Docker Desktop daemon.
+
+## Configuration
+
+Copy `deployments/a2d2/.env.example` to `deployments/a2d2/.env` only if absent.
+Replace all five `CHANGE_ME_*` values with independent random hex secrets and
+restrict `.env` to mode 0600. The DB and AMQP URLs interpolate those passwords.
+Do not print, commit, or share the resulting env file. The session has already
+created this file; preserve it to retain access to persistent volumes.
+
+The local entry URL is `http://127.0.0.1:3020`. The proxy binds only loopback.
+The project name below also isolates named volumes from existing services.
+
+```sh
+docker compose --project-directory . --env-file deployments/a2d2/.env \
+  -p a2d2-plane-full -f deployments/cli/community/docker-compose.yml \
+  -f deployments/a2d2/compose.source.yml config --quiet
+
+docker compose --project-directory . --env-file deployments/a2d2/.env \
+  -p a2d2-plane-full -f deployments/cli/community/docker-compose.yml \
+  -f deployments/a2d2/compose.source.yml up -d --build
+```
+
+The source override builds web, admin, space, live, backend, and proxy from this
+checkout. Worker, beat, and migrator use the same backend build. Upstream infrastructure
+images remain as declared upstream; this is not a fully digest-pinned release.
+The image suffix records the source baseline, not a verified successful build.
+
+## Native host contract
+
+The main window's native child WebView navigates to `/` as its own top-level page.
+It must have no A2D2 IPC capabilities. Host code owns persistent session isolation
+by A2D2 account, relay, and service. Plane's session and CSRF cookies stay in that
+WebView store; do not inject Buzz credentials or copy cookies across accounts.
+
+Caddy routes `/god-mode/` to admin, `/spaces/` to public space, `/live/` to live
+collaboration, `/api/` and `/auth/` to Django, and `/uploads/` to MinIO. Keep these
+routes and same-origin cookies intact. TLS/remote deployment is owned by the host
+and deployment integrator; this loopback configuration is not a remote deployment.
+
+Initialize the instance through `/god-mode/`, then exercise the original
+email/password login. API routes include `/auth/get-csrf-token/`, `/auth/sign-in/`,
+`/auth/sign-up/`, and `/auth/sign-out/`. SMTP-dependent magic links/password resets
+need instance email settings. OAuth provider routes exist but provider configuration,
+external navigation, popup handling, and native callback behavior require separate
+verification; none are claimed tested by this configuration.
+
+## Readiness and acceptance
+
+- `GET /` checks web delivery, not Django health.
+- `GET /api/instances/` checks the public instance API. HTTP 200 is insufficient:
+  inspect `is_activated` and `is_setup_done`; an empty instance also returns 200.
+- Django's health endpoint is internal `http://api:8000/` (the public root is web).
+- Verify migrator success and API, worker, beat, live logs.
+- In the native app, create a user/workspace/project/work item and upload a file;
+  close and reopen the child WebView and verify session/data persistence.
+- Restart this Compose project's services without deleting volumes, then verify
+  the saved work item and attachment again. Verify another account cannot access
+  private workspace data, and verify logout/account-switch store isolation.
+
+Compose validation is not login, persistence, or native integration verification.
+No volume deletion command is part of this workflow.
+
+Sources: `deployments/cli/community/docker-compose.yml`, `apps/proxy/Caddyfile.ce`,
+`apps/api/plane/urls.py`, `apps/api/plane/license/api/views/instance.py`,
+`apps/api/plane/authentication/urls.py`, `apps/api/plane/settings/common.py`.
+
+## Local backend architecture workaround
+
+On this Docker Desktop, upstream `python:3.12.12-alpine` ARM64 fails even
+`uname -m` with `exec format error`; plain Alpine ARM64 and Python AMD64 run.
+The override therefore selects `linux/amd64` for the four backend services only.
+This requires emulation on ARM hosts and may increase build/runtime cost. The
+Python base tag and original application Dockerfile remain unchanged.
+
+## Verification status (2026-09-16)
+
+Compose configuration passes. Backend is built once by `api` and shared by worker,
+beat, and migrator (six unique image builds total), avoiding concurrent exports to
+the same image name. The live TypeScript/build step passed, but image export failed
+with Docker containerd storage `input/output error`. Docker image listing and a
+previously working Alpine container then failed with the same storage read error.
+Host storage reported 15 GiB available and 100% capacity. The exact storage failure
+cause is not yet established. No application login/save/restart validation passed;
+restore Docker storage health or use another Docker host before resuming. No prune,
+reset, or volume deletion was performed.
