+# Plane remote Linux amd64 handoff
+
+Source: makeplane/plane commit `2f895b82dad839c730c36a5c0cbc046f1e5d6b56`.
+Existing worktree: `REPOS/plane-native-runtime`, branch `a2d2/plane-native-runtime`.
+The deployment additions are uncommitted; transfer `deployments/a2d2/` explicitly,
+excluding `.env` and any generated lock/temp files. Do not transfer local Docker data.
+Local Docker is stopped for this task: no build, pull, restart, prune, or volume changes.
+
+## Destination and secrets
+
+Integrator supplies the Linux amd64 host and HTTPS origin. Install git, Python 3,
+Docker Engine, and Compose with `!override` / `!reset` support. Verify disk and
+memory headroom before building; this session has no measured minimum capacity.
+Check out the exact source commit and copy these deployment additions.
+Use a new `a2d2-plane-full` project only after checking that name is unused on the
+remote host. Keep source and `.env` access restricted to deployment operators.
+
+Copy `.env.example` to `.env` only if absent; chmod 0600. Set five independent
+random hex secrets: POSTGRES_PASSWORD, RABBITMQ_PASSWORD, AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY,
+SECRET_KEY, LIVE_SERVER_SECRET_KEY. Never replace credentials for existing volumes.
+Other variable names are exhaustively listed in `.env.example`; DATABASE_URL and
+AMQP_URL reference their passwords through Compose interpolation. AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID
+is the MinIO username. Keep internal API_BASE_URL and AWS_S3_ENDPOINT_URL unchanged.
+
+Set WEB_URL and CORS_ALLOWED_ORIGINS to the final HTTPS origin; APP_DOMAIN to its
+hostname. Keep SITE_ADDRESS=:80. The supplied proxy remains 127.0.0.1:3020:80 on
+that remote machine. The integrator terminates TLS in a host reverse proxy and
+forwards the complete origin, including WebSockets, to that loopback port. The
+host proxy must overwrite forwarded headers. A containerized ingress needs a
+separate explicitly designed network route; its own loopback is not the host.
+Do not expose database, queue, Redis, or MinIO ports. The remote host loopback URL
+cannot be used directly by a WebView running on the user's machine.
+
+## Remote-only build and image freeze
+
+Run from repository root on the selected remote host, using Bash. These commands
+are preparation instructions, not evidence that deployment has succeeded.
+
+```bash
+set -euo pipefail
+umask 077
+test "$(uname -s)" = Linux
+test "$(uname -m)" = x86_64
+test "$(git rev-parse HEAD)" = 2f895b82dad839c730c36a5c0cbc046f1e5d6b56
+# Before running: ensure no tracked source edits and no CHANGE_ME values in .env.
+git diff --exit-code HEAD -- . ':!deployments/a2d2'
+if grep -q CHANGE_ME deployments/a2d2/.env; then exit 1; fi
+plane_compose=(docker compose --project-directory . --env-file deployments/a2d2/.env
+  -p a2d2-plane-full -f deployments/cli/community/docker-compose.yml
+  -f deployments/a2d2/compose.source.yml -f deployments/a2d2/compose.amd64.yml)
+"${plane_compose[@]}" config --quiet
+"${plane_compose[@]}" pull plane-db plane-redis plane-mq plane-minio
+"${plane_compose[@]}" build web admin space live api proxy
+# Never persist config JSON: it contains interpolated secrets.
+test ! -e deployments/a2d2/compose.images.lock.yml
+"${plane_compose[@]}" config --format json |
+  python3 deployments/a2d2/lock-images.py > deployments/a2d2/compose.images.lock.yml.tmp
+mv deployments/a2d2/compose.images.lock.yml.tmp deployments/a2d2/compose.images.lock.yml
+plane_locked=("${plane_compose[@]}" -f deployments/a2d2/compose.images.lock.yml)
+"${plane_locked[@]}" config --quiet
+# Migrations must succeed before API/workers are launched.
+"${plane_locked[@]}" up -d plane-db plane-redis plane-mq plane-minio
+"${plane_locked[@]}" run --rm migrator
+"${plane_locked[@]}" up -d --no-build --pull never
+"${plane_locked[@]}" ps -a
+python3 deployments/a2d2/verify-origin.py https://REPLACE_WITH_PLANE_HOST
+```
+
+There is currently NO successful app image/digest to hand off. Source tags
+`a2d2-plane-{web,admin,space,live,backend,proxy}:2f895b82da` are build labels,
+not content locks. Infrastructure currently comes from upstream postgres:15.7-alpine,
+valkey/valkey:7.2.11-alpine, rabbitmq:3.13.6-management-alpine, minio/minio:latest.
+The first successful remote build/pull resolves these moving inputs; lock-images.py
+then checks every image is Linux amd64 and freezes all 13 services to local SHA256
+image IDs, removes build configuration and prevents pulls. This pins deployment
+artifacts on that host, not reproducible future source builds. Keep these images;
+a new host requires docker save/load or registry publication with repo digests.
+Do not claim registry digest pinning from a local image ID.
+
+## Acceptance and preservation
+
+1. Verify all expected services and migrator exit status; inspect private logs for
+   API/worker/beat/live/proxy failures. Internal Django health: use api container
+   Python urllib to GET http://127.0.0.1:8000/. Public `/` is the web UI.
+2. Run verify-origin.py before/after `/god-mode/` initialization. It exits 2 if setup
+   remains incomplete, 0 only for the origin smoke. Source instance.py returns flat
+   flags when no instance exists, but `{config, instance}` after creation; inspect
+   nested `instance.is_setup_done`, not a presumed top-level `is_activated`.
+3. In the real A2D2 child WebView, email/password login, create a private workspace,
+   project and unique work item, and upload a file. Record IDs and file checksum
+   privately. Close/reopen and verify login/session and contents.
+4. Restart ONLY this project with `"${plane_locked[@]}" restart`. Log in again and
+   verify the same item and attachment checksum. A successful smoke is insufficient.
+5. Verify a second account cannot read the private item; verify logout/account
+   switch isolates cookies. OAuth and email flows require separate provider setup.
+
+Do not run down -v, prune, reset, or delete existing files/volumes. Remote first
+startup creates new data; existing local volumes remain preserved and are NOT
